      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(1)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Note that we need the answer in radians. Using a calculator in \"radians\" mode, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(1)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}≈1.850\\,815…≈1.851\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
