    "q-123545": {
      "dom_id": "step-q123545",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{57}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{19\\pi }{60})$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{8\\pi }{35})$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{14}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{80})$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Converting ${57}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{57}^{∘}=57\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{19\\pi }{60}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Converting ${32}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{32}^{∘}=32\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{8\\pi }{45}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{8\\pi }{45}\\ne \\frac{8\\pi }{35}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Converting ${14}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{14}^{∘}=14\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{7\\pi }{90}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{7\\pi }{90}\\ne \\frac{7\\pi }{80}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is 'I only'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
