    "q-123550": {
      "dom_id": "step-q123550",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡{22}^{∘}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{90})$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡{94}^{∘}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{37\\pi }{90})$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡{76}^{∘}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{19\\pi }{25})$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Converting ${22}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{22}^{∘}=22\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{11\\pi }{90}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Converting ${94}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{94}^{∘}=94\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{47\\pi }{90}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{47\\pi }{90}\\ne \\frac{37\\pi }{90}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Converting ${76}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get \n\n$$\n{76}^{∘}=76\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{19\\pi }{45}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{19\\pi }{45}\\ne \\frac{19\\pi }{25}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is 'I only'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
