    "q-123549": {
      "dom_id": "step-q123549",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{cot}⁡{20}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{9})$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{cot}⁡{50}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{18})$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{cot}⁡{80}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{9})$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Converting ${20}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get \n\n$$\n{20}^{∘}=20\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{\\pi }{9}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Converting ${50}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get \n\n$$\n{50}^{∘}=50\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{5\\pi }{18}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Converting ${80}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get \n\n$$\n{80}^{∘}=80\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{4\\pi }{9}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{4\\pi }{9}\\ne \\frac{2\\pi }{9}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is 'I and II only'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
