      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{20}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{36})$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{35}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{36})$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Converting ${15}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{15}^{∘}=15\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Converting ${20}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get\n\n$$\n{20}^{∘}=20\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{\\pi }{9}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nThe statement is false because $\\frac{\\pi }{9}\\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{36}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Converting ${35}^{∘}$ from degrees to radians, we get \n\n$$\n{35}^{∘}=35\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{180}=\\frac{7\\pi }{36}\\,\\text{radians}.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is 'I and III only'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
